    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205104": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Philosophy",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Adjunct, Philosophy Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct, Philosophy Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct, Philosophy Category: Academic / Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Philosophy Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 205104 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: CONTRACT TYPE: Semester based. BASIC FUNCTION: The Department of Philosophy is seeking a Spring 2027 adjunct faculty to teach several sections of PHL 105 Finding Your Moral Compass, an introductory philosophical ethics course required of all Salve Regina students. Courses will be held in-person on our campus in Newport, RI. PHL 105: Finding Your Moral Compass (3 Credits) Fulfills Core Requirement in First Year Foundational Courses Salve Regina University \"encourages students to work for a world that is harmonious, just, and merciful.\" To that end, this course will equip you with the philosophical tools of moral reasoning needed to navigate ethical challenges in pursuit of a life well-lived. We'll explore the question of what constitutes \"goodness\" and how to make just decisions that help in developing your own virtuous character while fostering harmonious communities grounded in mercy. By delving into core ethical theories like virtue ethics, deontology, utilitarianism, and natural law, you'll gain the ability to critically analyze arguments, formulate well-reasoned positions, and develop your own ethical framework. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Prepare and teach in-person, on-campus classes Prepare, proctor and grade examinations Grade and return student assignments, examinations, reports, etc. in a timely manner Provide a course syllabus at the start of the semester to the department chair (A template will be provided by the department chair.) Basic use of the Canvas learning management system to disseminate syllabus, and other course material to students. (Help using this system is available, if needed.) Hold weekly office hours Use Salve email (i.e., @salve.edu) to send and receive official email correspondence with students, staff, and administrators. Requirements: A minimum of a master's degree in philosophy, along with teaching experience In ability to teach in-person classes at the scheduled class times Additional Information: Salve Regina University strives to provide equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, marital or parental status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal or state law, in the administration of Salve Regina's employment policies, education policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other University administered programs. In accordance with Title IX, it does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any of its educational programs or activities. Salve Regina is also committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    },
    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204892": {
      "title": "Adjunct, History",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Adjunct, History Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct, History Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct, History Category: Academic / Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: History Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 204892 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: CONTRACT TYPE:  Semester based. Job Description: The Department of History is seeking adjunct faculty to teach sections of HIS 113: U.S. History to 1877 and HIS 114: U.S. History since 1877. Courses will be held in-person on our campus in Newport, RI. HIS 113:  History of the United States to 1877 (3 Credits) This survey course covers political, social, religious, economic and cultural trends in America from the Jamestown settlement in 1607 through the Civil War and Reconstruction. Topics include the development of slavery, concepts of religious freedom, industrialization and westward expansion. Special attention is paid to the role Newport played in the Colonial and Revolutionary period. HIS 114:  History of the United States since 1877 (3 Credits) This survey course covers political, social, religious, economic and cultural trends in America from the end of Reconstruction through the end of the Cold War. Topics include America's rise as a world power, Progressivism, the women's movement and the civil rights movement. Special attention is paid to the role that Newport played during the Gilded Age. Requirements: Required : A minimum of a master's degree in history, along with college-level teaching experience Teach in-person, on-campus classes at the scheduled class times Prepare, proctor and grade examinations Grade and return student assignments, examinations, etc. in a timely manner Provide a course syllabus at the start of the semester using the Simple Syllabus program Basic use of the Canvas learning management system to disseminate syllabus, and other course material to students. (Help using this system is available, if needed.) Hold weekly office hours (1 hour minimum) Use Salve email (i.e., @salve.edu) to send and receive official email correspondence with students, staff, and administrators. Preferred : Ph.D. in history strongly preferred Additional Information: Salve Regina University strives to provide equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, marital or parental status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal or state law, in the administration of Salve Regina's employment policies, education policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other University administered programs. In accordance with Title IX, it does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any of its educational programs or activities. Salve Regina is also committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
    },
    "https://salve.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203610": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Dance",
      "description": "Salve Regina University\nJob Posting: Adjunct, Dance Salve Regina University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct, Dance Title Home About Employment Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct, Dance Category: Academic / Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Dance Locations: Newport, RI Posted: Aug 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position ID: 203610 Share About Salve Regina University: Salve Regina University, ranked as one of the most transformative colleges in the United States by Money Magazine, is a comprehensive Catholic University located in the scenic coastal community of Newport, Rhode Island. The University's commitment to academic success and personal discovery extends beyond its historic campus into a dynamic world where the application of higher thinking and skill are most valued. Salve Regina offers bachelor's and master's degree programs, graduate certificates, and doctoral programs in humanities, international relations and nursing. Enrollment includes more than 2,600 undergraduate and graduate students from across the U.S. and around the world. Job Description: The Department of Music, Theatre and Dance seeks part-time instructors to teach undergraduate courses in Theatre and Dance. Applicants are added to the pool list throughout the year. Appointments are made on a semester-by-semester (fall/spring) basis with opportunities for long-term part-time employment. Hiring decisions are made in late-spring/early summer for the fall semester, and early fall for the spring semester. In alignment with the mission of Salve Regina University, the Department of Music, Theatre and Dance is committed to cultivating graduates with enduring values that enhance their ability to think critically, respond creatively, and actively promote universal justice. Preference will be given to applicants with a demonstrated record of social consciousness. We encourage applicants who will contribute to the diversity of our university community, including members of historically underrepresented groups. Instructors with expertise in the following areas are encouraged to apply: Vogue Waacking West African Dance Jazz Dance styles rooted in Africanist aesthetics Hip Hop Tap Salsa Requirements: Required : MA or MFA with professional teaching experience. A BA or BFA without an MA/MFA will be considered for studio course instruction if the candidate has equivalent performance and/or teaching experience. Additional Information: Salve Regina University strives to provide equal opportunity in employment and education to all employees, students and applicants. No employee, student or applicant shall be discriminated against or harassed on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, marital or parental status, military or veteran status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal or state law, in the administration of Salve Regina's employment policies, education policies, admission policies, scholarship and loan programs, athletic and other University administered programs. In accordance with Title IX, it does not discriminate on the basis of sex in any of its educational programs or activities. Salve Regina is also committed to making its programs and campus accessible to its visitors and compliant with all applicable non-discrimination laws. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online for any open staff and faculty positions by providing a cover-letter and resume. Pre-employment background checks and reference checks are required of successful candidates. Salve Regina University participates in E-verify. Please provide three professional references (1 current/former supervisor, 2 colleagues). If you are selected as one of our finalists applicants for the position, we will request the referee's you listed in your application to complete a reference screening form. By adding your referee's contact information below, you consent to allow Salve Regina University to contact your referee's for written references. URL: www.salve.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Salve Regina University 100 Ochre Point Avenue Newport, Rhode Island 02840"
